To extract traces of neuronal voltage activity, we first used an algorithm, NoRMCorre52, to correct computationally the raw (1 kHz) fluorescence videos (see the High-speed fluorescence voltage imaging section above) for lateral displacements of the brain. To improve the signal-to-noise ratios of the videos, we applied a denoising algorithm that was based on a singular value decomposition. This involved first reshaping the raw video into a matrix, \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
